-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/sell/home-value/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is my home worth in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on what similar homes near yours sold for in the last few months, adjusted for condition, upgrades, and location details like water and golf. A licensed agent builds that comparison, called a CMA, from MLS sold records. We prepare one free for any Grand Strand address."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are online home value estimates accurate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"They are a useful starting point. They work from public records, so they cannot see the view, the condition, the building's health, or whether a condo finances normally. A CMA checks the estimate against real sold homes. Start online, then confirm the number before you price."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a CMA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A comparative market analysis. An agent pulls the recent sold homes most like yours from the MLS, adjusts for the differences, and lands on a realistic price range. It is the pricing tool listing agents use to set a list price."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between a CMA and an appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An appraisal is a formal valuation a lender orders during a purchase, done by a licensed appraiser for a fee. A CMA is a pricing analysis an agent prepares, usually free, to set a listing price. Both work from sold comparable homes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a home valuation cost anything?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Ours is free, and there is no obligation to list with us."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How fast will I get my home's value?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We reach out the same day you send the form, evenings included, and the full analysis follows quickly, usually within a day or two."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should I get a valuation if I am not selling yet?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Knowing the real number helps with insurance, tax decisions, and timing, and many owners check it yearly. We will give you the figure either way."}}]}</script>
