+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is my home worth in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Across Horry County, houses and other homes resold for a middle price of about $350,000 in the latest 12 months of county deeds, and condos for about $215,000. In the city of Conway the middle house sold for about $265,000, and inside North Myrtle Beach for about $535,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How accurate are online home estimates in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Close on some homes and far off on others. Redfin's figures for Horry County put its middle miss at 6.6 percent on homes not for sale, and 1.65 percent once a home is listed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between a CMA and an appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A CMA, a comparative market analysis, is an agent's pricing of your home from the sales most like it. An appraisal is a licensed appraiser's opinion of value. In South Carolina an agent's valuation must not be called an appraisal."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why is my county assessed value different from my market value?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The county values every home at once, for tax, so it cannot see what one home has. The taxable value is often lower still: under state law it can rise only so far between sales. A sale resets it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are Myrtle Beach home prices dropping?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. By the Federal Housing Finance Agency's house price index, house prices in Horry County were about flat in the year to mid-2026, after rising about half from mid-2021 to mid-2025."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does a home valuation cost anything?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Our valuation is free, and you do not have to list your home with us."}}]}</script>
