-</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The method</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">How we price your home</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Start anywhere you like, including the online estimates. They are a useful first look at the market.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The finished number comes from a comparative market analysis, a CMA. We pull the homes most like yours that sold in roughly the last three to six months, adjust for the differences that matter, and land on a realistic range plus a pricing strategy for the season.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;">The number comes with the reasoning. We show you the exact sold homes behind it, so you can judge the comparison yourself.</p><div style="background:var(--ivory);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.2rem 1.3rem;margin-top:1.8rem;max-width:720px;display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between"><p style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600">Want us to look at it for you?</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass" href="#lead-form">Get my home value</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">What moves the number</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">What moves your home&#39;s value in Myrtle Beach</h2><ul style="list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.7rem;margin:1.4rem 0 0;padding:0;max-width:720px"><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Location and water.</strong> Ocean, Intracoastal, creek, golf, and even which way a condo faces. The same floor plan prices differently by view.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Condition and the big systems.</strong> Kitchens and baths, and the age of the roof and HVAC. Buyers here price salt-air wear into every offer.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">HOA health on condos.</strong> Dues, reserves, insurance, and litigation all show up in the price, because they decide which buyers can even finance the building. That financing status is explained in our guide to <a href="/invest/non-warrantable-condos/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">non-warrantable condos</a>.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">The buyer&#39;s tax status.</strong> A primary resident pays the 4 percent property tax rate and a second-home or rental buyer pays 6 percent, which changes what each will pay for the same house. Details on the <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">property tax page</a>.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Insurance costs.</strong> Coastal insurance is a real monthly line, and buyers price it in. See <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">coastal insurance costs</a>.</span></li><li style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6"><span style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:700">&#10003;</span><span><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Season and timing.</strong> Spring sales move fastest here. The best month for speed is not always the best month for price, which is part of the pricing strategy we bring with the CMA.</span></li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The details that change the price</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">What public records cannot tell you</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Public records list beds, baths, and square feet. They do not show the ocean view, the renovated kitchen, the building&#39;s reserve fund, or whether the condo next door just sold as a non-warrantable unit. In this market those details move prices by tens of thousands of dollars.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;">That is why the same floor plan can carry two different values, and why we verify every number against actual sold homes before you price yours.</p><div style="background:var(--ivory);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.2rem 1.3rem;margin-top:1.8rem;max-width:720px;display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between"><p style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600">Want us to look at it for you?</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass" href="#lead-form">Get my home value</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">If you are selling</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">From number to plan</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The value is step one. Step two is what you keep. Our <a href="/sell/net-proceeds/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">net proceeds calculator</a> turns the price into your walk-away number after commission, deed stamps, and closing costs, and the <a href="/sell/capital-gains/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">capital gains page</a> covers the tax side.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;">The full selling process, timeline, and marketing plan live on our <a href="/sell/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">selling page</a>. Thinking about selling it yourself? We coach FSBO sellers too, details on the <a href="/sell/fsbo/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">for sale by owner page</a>. We will build your free valuation either way.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy)"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;padding:3rem 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.9rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:.8rem">Ready for your number?</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.6);max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 1.6rem;line-height:1.7">Send the address. You get the analysis and the reasoning behind it. You keep the decision.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.75rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="#lead-form">Get my free home value</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135" style="color:var(--ivory);border-color:rgba(244,239,232,.4)">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Home value FAQ</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is my home worth in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">It depends on what similar homes near yours sold for in the last few months, adjusted for condition, upgrades, and location details like water and golf. A licensed agent builds that comparison, called a CMA, from MLS sold records. We prepare one free for any Grand Strand address.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Are online home value estimates accurate?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">They are a useful starting point. They work from public records, so they cannot see the view, the condition, the building's health, or whether a condo finances normally. A CMA checks the estimate against real sold homes. Start online, then confirm the number before you price.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is a CMA?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A comparative market analysis. An agent pulls the recent sold homes most like yours from the MLS, adjusts for the differences, and lands on a realistic price range. It is the pricing tool listing agents use to set a list price.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is the difference between a CMA and an appraisal?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">An appraisal is a formal valuation a lender orders during a purchase, done by a licensed appraiser for a fee. A CMA is a pricing analysis an agent prepares, usually free, to set a listing price. Both work from sold comparable homes.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Does a home valuation cost anything?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">No. Ours is free, and there is no obligation to list with us.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How fast will I get my home's value?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">We reach out the same day you send the form, evenings included, and the full analysis follows quickly, usually within a day or two.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Should I get a valuation if I am not selling yet?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes. Knowing the real number helps with insurance, tax decisions, and timing, and many owners check it yearly. We will give you the figure either way.</p></div></div></section>
